{
  "description": "Reactive-agent ecology under a fundamental SHOCK. The market equilibrates with the mid tracking just below the oracle fundamental (value traders perpetually buying to close the gap). A DOWNWARD scheduled_jump drives the fundamental below the mid, FLIPPING value traders from buying to selling; the resulting price decline is chased by momentum traders (threshold 1) while market makers re-quote a thin ladder \u2014 a causal selling cascade a static-batched / vmap-over-books port cannot reproduce. Pre-jump the intervention is RNG-neutral (byte-identical to the no-jump baseline); the post-jump reactive response is the sealed answer. Density is tuned to keep a 7s horizon under the correctness size cap (no horizon auto-scale, so the jump always fires) and the book two-sided.",
